          "id": null,
          "classes": [
            "fx-info-i"
          ],
          "label": "Uses AHD interpolation, which cleans up dense green/magenta false-color speckle on sunlit water/specular highlights much further than Standard — but it trades away some general chroma-noise headroom elsewhere in the frame, so it's opt-in per photo rather than a global default. Requires reopening this photo to take effect. Desktop only.",
          "dynamic": false,
          "familyMembership": [
            "button",
            "info-button",
            "toggle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "chromasmith-22.html:1933:info-button",
          "source": "chromasmith-22.html",
          "line": 1933,
          "tag": "button",
          "selector": ".fx-info-i",
          "id": null,
          "classes": [
            "fx-info-i"
          ],
          "label": "Bright specular highlights (sunlit water, glints) sometimes show green/magenta demosaic false-color that no amount of Luminance/Color NR fully removes. Since real highlight color is usually near-neutral anyway, this fades Cb/Cr toward zero from mid-tones (~45%) up through highlights — reaches far enough to cover where the fringing actually sits, so it WILL flatten real color in bright areas too at high amounts. Per-photo only, so it never touches other images.",
          "dynamic": false,
          "familyMembership": [
            "button",
            "control-row",
            "info-button",
            "slider"
          ]
        },
